  "goodToKnow": "Das Jobcenter is the local office for people receiving Bürgergeld (called Hartz IV until 2023), the basic income support for long-term unemployed and low earners. Short-term unemployment benefit, Arbeitslosengeld, is handled by the separate Agentur für Arbeit. Jobcenters were created by the Hartz reforms of 2005. It's a pseudo-English word pronounced roughly DSHOP-sen-ter. Plural: die Jobcenter."
